  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Diisobutylaluminium hydride, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AlH</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Bu</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;also known as DIBAL or DIBAL-H, is an exceedingly useful and versatile reducing agent. It is an electrophilic reducing agent, usually employed in selective reductions of esters or nitriles to aldehydes</p><p>So, in first step nitrile group will be reduced to aldehyde group.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c28ff58c-e447-4e6f-acf7-c45ba8d86919-image.png\" style=\"width: 513px; height: 170px;\" /></p><p>In second step cross aldol condensation reaction will take place which will give mixture of products. Out of which one of the product will be option B.</p></blockquote>",
